<section id="sync" class="sync-section section-shell" aria-labelledby="sync-heading" data-tone="sky">
        <header class="section-heading heading-group"><p class="eyebrow">Your data, your choice</p>
          <h2 id="sync-heading" class="phrase-reveal" aria-label="Sync with anything. Answer to no one.">
          <span class="heading-phrase color-phrase" aria-hidden="true" style="--phrase-order:0">Sync with anything.</span><br>
          <span class="heading-phrase" aria-hidden="true" style="--phrase-order:1">Answer to no one.</span>
        </h2>
          <p>Your data, your choice. Keep it close or take it with you.<br class="desktop-break"> You decide where your notes call home.</p></header>
        <div class="sync-options">
          <div class="sync-option"><article><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#device-icon"/></svg><h3>Local</h3><p>Keep your data on your device and sync using the local file system. Designed for maximum privacy.</p><span class="option-state"><i></i>On your terms</span></article></div>
          <div class="sync-option"><article><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#github-icon"/></svg><h3>GitHub</h3><p>Sync with a private GitHub repository. Changes sync instantly via HTTP, with no manual commits. Works on mobile, too.</p><a class="text-link" href="/docs/syncing-with-github/">How it works <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article></div>
          <div class="sync-option"><article><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#server-icon"/></svg><h3>Self-hosted</h3><p>Run your own backend and stay fully in control. For when ownership, privacy, and cross-device sync matter most.</p><span class="badge">Coming soon</span></article></div>
          <div class="sync-option"><article><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#cloud-icon"/></svg><h3>Snippets Cloud</h3><p>Automatic, cross-device syncing. Everything up to date everywhere, with zero setup or maintenance.</p><span class="badge">Coming soon</span></article></div>
        </div>
        <div class="export-note"><span class="markdown-mark" aria-hidden="true">M<span>↓</span></span><p><strong>Export to Markdown.</strong> Avoid vendor lock-in. Keep your data forever.</p></div>
      </section>
